{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An interval tree: a sorted collection of half-open intervals with a value each, which finds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intervals overlapping a range, containing a point, or lying within a range in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"k"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" + 1) log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") for "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" results."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntervalTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bound","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The intervals are kept in an AVL tree ordered by lower bound, then upper bound, then the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were inserted in, and each vertex also records the largest upper bound in its subtree, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a search skips every subtree that ends before the query begins (Cormen, Leiserson, Rivest and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Stein, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Introduction to Algorithms","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", §14.3). The same interval may be stored more than once,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with different values."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var meetings = IntervalTree<Int, String>()","meetings.insert(9 ..< 10, value: \"stand-up\")","meetings.insert(10 ..< 12, value: \"design review\")","meetings.insert(11 ..< 13, value: \"lunch\")","meetings.containing(11).map(\\.value)          \/\/ [\"design review\", \"lunch\"]","meetings.overlapping(9 ..< 11).map(\\.value)   \/\/ [\"stand-up\", \"design review\"]","meetings.contained(in: 9 ..< 12).map(\\.range) \/\/ [9 ..< 10, 10 ..< 12]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intervals are half-open, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"9 ..< 10"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"10 ..< 12"},{"type":"text","text":" touch without overlapping. As a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection, the tree’s elements are its entries in that order, read by in-order position."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/intervaltree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/Entry","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/IntervalTree\/